What the workflow is now
Read the 6 open recovery reviews in Jira → settle in GitHub which repo and release actually serves each one and whether the fix really passed CI → land 1 of 4 statuses (was 7) → allocate up to 2 windows on the Sheets tracker → leave 1 comment per incident and 1 unsent Gmail draft. Three write actions in three apps.

The decision traps all survive: the PaymentRecovery decoy pair, the wrong repo and tag on IRM-1, the quoted PR numbers that match nothing, the Jira comment claiming "all green" against a failed integration-tests run, the rollback that drops rows written after its migration, and the Inactive contact row.

One structural change worth knowing: the run now writes its decision as a Jira comment and leaves the description and status alone. That keeps the seeded traps unspent, which is why reset.txt is down to deleting comments, clearing 2 cells, and deleting 1 draft.

Expected run: INC-2042 takes W-01 (its workaround expires first), INC-2041 takes W-02, INC-2045 drops to Scheduled on capacity, INC-2043 and INC-2044 hold for different reasons, INC-2046 is No Release Required, W-06 comes back unused.

